From 4886bddbe77e0f1dc089785c761f5ed46284a2d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:45:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Material properties: version 3 of the functions of batches of
 points

- copies of the data structures of version 3 of TFEL, with the same members
  in the same order: mgis_mp_BatchStatistics (opaque keys),
  mgis_mp_BatchExecutionOptions (formerly mgis_mp_ExecutionOptions),
  mgis_mp_BatchConstField, mgis_mp_BatchField, mgis_mp_BatchData,
  mgis_mp_BatchOutputStatus (first unreliable point), the types of the
  pointers to the functions (mgis_mp_BatchReportFctPtr takes no policy) and
  mgis_mp_initializeBatchStatistics. The offset of each member is checked
  against TFEL, and the initialization of the statistics is compared bit for
  bit;
- load makes two independent tests: the functions of batches of points
  (S_generic_parallel and S_generic_parallel_report) are loaded if the
  library exports their version, the function of a point if the material
  property has been generated by the generic interface. An error is reported
  if the library provides none of them. The description gives the version
  of the functions of batches of points (batch_api_version), and
  isGenericParallelMaterialProperty tells if they are loaded;
- the evaluation builds the data of the batch. The errors of the batch
  (-5, -6, -7) are reported by exceptions.
