-When a material property generated by the `generic-parallel` interface is
-loaded, `MGIS` reads the version of its functions, its backend and its
-memory space, and loads the function evaluating a set of points
-(`batch_fct` member) instead of the function evaluating one point (`fct`
-member). `isGenericParallelMaterialProperty` tells if a material property
-evaluates sets of points.
+When a material property is loaded, `MGIS` makes two independent tests:
+
+- if the library exports the version of the functions of batches of points
+  (`<name>_generic_parallel_api_version` symbol), `MGIS` checks this
+  version (`MGIS_MP_GENERIC_PARALLEL_API_VERSION`), reads the backend and
+  the memory space, and loads the function evaluating a batch of points
+  (`batch_fct` member) and the function analysing the statistics of an
+  evaluation (`batch_report_fct` member);
+- if the material property has been generated by the `generic` interface
+  (`<name>_mfront_interface` symbol equal to `Generic`, or absent for the
+  versions of `TFEL` older than 4.1), `MGIS` loads the function evaluating
+  one point (`fct` member).
+
+An error is reported if the library provides none of those functions.
+`isGenericParallelMaterialProperty` tells if a material property has the
+functions of batches of points. The data structures of those functions
+are copies of the ones of `TFEL`, with the same members in the same
+order (`mgis_mp_BatchData`, `mgis_mp_BatchOutputStatus`, etc., declared
+in `MGIS/MaterialProperty/BatchMaterialPropertyFctPtr.hxx`).
 
