 The evaluation point by point stops at the first failure, whereas a
-`generic-parallel` material property evaluates all the points. The index
-of the first point where the evaluation failed is the same. The status
-and `bounds_status` of a `generic-parallel` material property describe
-the first failed check over all the points, in a fixed order (invalid
-result, physical bounds, bounds, the variables in order), which does not
-depend on the order of the computations. The evaluation point by point
-reports the check of the first point. They differ only if several kinds
-of failures occur.
+`generic-parallel` material property evaluates all the points (the output
+is `NaN` at the points where a bound makes the evaluation fail, and the
+computed value where the result is not finite). The index of the first
+point where the evaluation failed is the same, and the status and
+`bounds_status` describe the check retained at this point, as for the
+evaluation point by point, except that `bounds_status` is null for a
+result which is not finite (status `-4`), even if a bound is violated
+with the warning policy at this point. Without failure, they describe the
+first point where the result is unreliable.
 
